[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Our Neighbour, the River]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.32]Lesson 56 | 第56课
[00:02.55]Our neighbour, the river | 我们的邻居——河流
[00:09.41]Why had the neighbours left their farm? | 邻居们为什么离开了他们的农场？
[00:13.91]The river which forms the eastern boundary of our farm has always played an important part in our lives. | 形成我们农场东边界的河流，一直在我们的生活中发挥着重要作用。
[00:21.26]Without it we could not make a living. | 没有它我们就无法谋生。
[00:24.33]There is only enough spring water to supply the needs of the house so we have to pump from the river for farm use. | 泉水仅够供应生活用水，因此农活用水只得从河里抽取。
[00:32.59]We tell the river all our secrets. | 我们把所有的心事都告诉这条河。
[00:35.36]We know instinctively, just as beekeepers with their bees, | 我们本能地知道，就像养蜂人同他们的蜜蜂那样，
[00:39.98]that misfortune might overtake us if the important events of our lives were not related to it. | 如果不把生活中的大事告诉它，灾祸就可能降临到我们头上。
[00:48.62]We have special river birthday parties in the summer. | 夏天，我们为河流举办特别的生日聚会。
[00:52.63]Sometimes we go upstream to a favourite backwater, | 有时我们逆流而上，到一处最喜爱的回流区，
[00:56.49]sometimes we have our party at the boathouse, | 有时我们在船屋里聚会，
[00:59.61]which a predecessor of ours at the farm built in the meadow hard by the deepest pool for swimming and diving. | 船屋是我们的农场前辈在深水潭旁的草地上建造的，专供游泳和跳水之用。
[01:07.74]In a heat wave we choose a midnight birthday party and that is the most exciting of all. | 热浪袭来时，我们就选择午夜举行生日聚会，那是最令人兴奋的。
[01:14.50]We welcome the seasons by the riverside, crowning the youngest girl with flowers in the spring, | 我们在河边迎接四季：春天给最小的姑娘戴上花冠，
[01:21.08]holding a summer festival on Midsummer Eve, giving thanks for the harvest in the autumn, and throwing a holly wreath into the current in the winter. | 仲夏之夜举行夏至节，秋天为丰收感恩，冬天把冬青枝环抛入激流。
[01:32.66]After a long period of rain the river may overflow its banks. | 在长时间降雨之后，河水可能漫过堤岸。
[01:37.93]This is a rare occurrence as our climate seldom goes to extremes. | 这种情况很少发生，因为我们的气候很少走极端。
[01:43.11]We are lucky in that only the lower fields, | 我们很幸运，只有低洼的田地
[01:46.40]which make up a very small proportion of our farm, are affected by flooding, | ——它们只占农场的很小一部分——会受到洪水的影响，
[01:51.73]but other farms are less favourably sited, and flooding can sometimes spell disaster for their owners. | 但其他农场的位置就没有这么有利了，洪水有时会给农场主带来灾难。
[02:00.33]One bad winter we watched the river creep up the lower meadows. | 有一个糟糕的冬天，我们眼看着河水漫上低洼的草地。
[02:06.04]All the cattle had been moved into stalls and we stood to lose little. | 所有的牲畜都已转入畜栏，我们不会损失什么。
[02:11.01]We were, however, worried about our nearest neighbours, whose farm was low lying and who were newcomers to the district. | 然而，我们为最近的邻居担忧，他们的农场地势低洼，而且又是新迁到这个地区来的。
[02:20.08]As the floods had put the telephone out of order, we could not find out how they were managing. | 洪水使电话出了故障，我们无法了解他们的处境。
[02:26.30]From an attic window we could get a sweeping view of the river where their land joined ours, | 从顶楼的窗口，我们可以一览无余地看到两家的土地相接处的河面，
[02:32.65]and at the most critical juncture we took turns in watching that point. | 在最危急的关头，我们轮流监视那个地点。
[02:37.80]The first sign of disaster was a dead sheep floating down. | 灾难的第一个迹象是一只死羊漂了下来。
[02:42.99]Next came a horse, swimming bravely, | 接着是一匹马，勇敢地游着水，
[02:46.07]but we were afraid that the strength of the current would prevent its landing anywhere before it became exhausted. | 但我们担心水流的冲力会使它在抵达任何地方之前就精疲力竭。
[02:53.85]Suddenly a raft appeared, looking rather like Noah's ark, carrying the whole family, a few hens, the dogs, a cat, and a bird in a cage. | 突然，一只筏子出现了，看上去颇像挪亚方舟，载着全家老小、几只母鸡、几条狗、一只猫和笼中的一只鸟。
[03:05.90]We realized that they must have become unduly frightened by the rising flood, | 我们意识到，他们一定是被不断上涨的洪水吓得惊慌失措，
[03:11.63]for their house, which had sound foundations, would have stood stoutly even if it had been almost submerged. | 因为他们的房子地基牢固，即使几乎被淹没，也会稳稳地挺立。
[03:20.42]The men of our family waded down through our flooded meadows with boat hooks, | 我们家的男人们拿着船钩，蹚过被洪水淹没的草地，
[03:25.34]in the hope of being able to grapple a corner of the raft and pull it out of the current towrds our bank. | 希望能钩住筏子的一角，把它拖离水流，弄到我们这一岸。
[03:33.53]We still think it a miracle that they were able to do so. | 至今我们仍认为他们能成功是个奇迹。
